{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonSector","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonSector","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Complex","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Analytic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.analyticAt_cpow_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.analyticAt_cpow_const","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonSector.lean#L85-L92","doc":"**Holomorphy of the fractional power** `z ↦ z^t` on the slit plane\n(`ℂ ∖ ℝ_{≤0}`), which contains every sector of opening `< 2π` about the\npositive axis. A direct instance of `AnalyticAt.cpow` (`z^t = exp(t log z)`,\n`log` analytic off the slit). The second geometric ingredient of the Watson\ncarrier, alongside `sector_cpow_mapsTo`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.sector_cpow_mapsTo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.sector_cpow_mapsTo","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonSector.lean#L77-L83","doc":"The sector `{z ≠ 0 : |arg z| < π/(2t)}` is mapped by `z ↦ z^t` into the open\nright half-plane `{re > 0}` — the `MapsTo` form the Watson transport\nconsumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.re_cpow_pos_of_abs_arg_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.re_cpow_pos_of_abs_arg_lt","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonSector.lean#L58-L75","doc":"**The fractional-power sector map (brick 4b-i).** For `0 < t` and `z ≠ 0` in\nthe sector `|arg z| < π/(2t)`, the fractional power `z^t` lands in the open\nright half-plane. Since the source sector has opening `π/t` (which is `> π`\nprecisely when `t < 1`), this is the opening-`>π` → half-plane contraction\nthe Watson transport needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.re_cpow_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.re_cpow_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonSector.lean#L43-L56","doc":"`Re(z^t) = ‖z‖^t · cos(t · arg z)` for `z ≠ 0` and real `t`: the real part\nof a fractional power, computed via `z^t = exp(log z · t)` and\n`Complex.exp_re`. No branch-cut `arg`-of-`cpow` identity needed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}